<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamanaka Yukimori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1545–1578</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Yamanaka Shikanosuke</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yamanaka Yukimori, also known as Yamanaka Shikanosuke, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> retainer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amago-clan">Amago clan</a> of Izumo. After the Mōri conquered the Amago in 1566 he led repeated attempts to restore the clan, latterly with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>. Captured when the Mōri took Kōzuki Castle in 1578, he was killed while being taken away as a prisoner, and he is celebrated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> as a model of loyalty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yamanaka-yukimori.jpg" alt="Yamanaka Yukimori" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yoshitoshi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akiyama_Buemon_-_Tsuki_hyakushi_-_Walters_95348.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
